  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combatting global security challenges through knowledge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project is to ensure that policy makers are equipped with up to date situational and political-economy analysis on emerging threats caused by transnational organized crime, that this reflects a diverse set of community voices and experiences, and can benefit from recommendations on relevant mitigating actions drawn from global best practice. 

The target group of the project are development and security policymakers in bilateral and multilateral systems and institutions working to protect communities made vulnerable by organized crime and criminal governance, corruption and illicit financial flows.  This particularly applies to vulnerable and marginalized populations in LDCs, fragile states and countries in conflict and with high levels of violence.</narrative>
  </description>
